 "roomNotes": {
  "Z01": "In this 3D proposal: a banyan bonsai on granite by the glass gate, three stones, handmade terracotta on the check-in desk and six terracotta plaques by a rural artist (placeholder; to be commissioned and credited). The approved logos and brand wall are unchanged.",
  "Z02": "In this 3D proposal: tea in clay cups on wooden trays, rural instruments above the console (ektara, dotara, banshi, dhol; makers to be identified), a small fig tree and ghritokumari, with the handloom pieces of the approved redesign.",
  "Z03": "In this 3D proposal: the Sun wall (sun, solar generation, use and storage, operations, with grid and backup shown) and a terracotta earth wall. Concept demonstration, not live factory data: \"Designed for a Solar-Powered Future\" until measured evidence exists.",
  "Z30": "In this 3D proposal: the Earth-to-Product gallery on the plinth (raw material, technique, prototype, testing, collection; the four forms are removed), living materials on the table, drinking water from a clay kolshi (source client-stated; no laboratory results yet) and a Future of Bengal lamp prototype by the boardroom door.",
  "Z08": "In this 3D proposal: clay cups at every place and a clay jug instead of glass, woven samples on wooden trays, and a bonsai in the corner by the screen.",
  "Z18": "In this 3D proposal: the only room with exterior windows: three bonsai and a tulsi pot take turns on the sunning shelf at window W10, a small fig tree by W09, and basket prototypes, woven samples and sketches on the co-creation table.",
  "Z12": "In this 3D proposal: tea in clay cups. The office itself is unchanged in this increment.",
  "Z07": "Option A only (the merchandising team moves first; owner decision). In this 3D proposal: the Green Uthan, a Bengali courtyard with a bot-tola seat around the column, two small fig trees and a bonsai under grow lights (no daylight here), stone seats and an open bamboo canopy; an artisan corner (Chakma back-strap loom and Marma weaving and basketry, both only with community consent; nakshi kantha, cane, painted terracotta); four room-sets for European buyers: living, dining, bedroom and hospitality. Every approved item that moves is in the relocation ledger.",
  "Z06": "Option A only (the accounts team moves first; owner decision). In this 3D proposal: the design education academy inside the existing glass accounts suite, 20 seats, a demonstration bench with a hands camera, a mobile screen and a pin-up board; the discussion room becomes the tutor room. The fire engineer sets the capacity.",
  "Z15": "In this 3D proposal: eight labelled boxes of natural materials on the low shelf (jute, hogla, cane, bamboo, water hyacinth, kaisa grass, coconut shell, terracotta) and Material Passport cards on the review table, their fields still to be documented. The D65 colour booth and the approved fabric library stay.",
  "Z16": "In this 3D proposal: a moisture and mould test set-up on the post-processing bench (sealed sample boxes, a scale, a moisture meter) with an empty test log. Methods to be agreed with an accredited laboratory; no results are shown. The 3D printers stay.",
  "Z17": "In this 3D proposal: cane and bamboo prototyping on the pattern table under a dust-extraction hood marked \"to be engineered\", and a steam-bending jig. The sample machines and forms stay. Seen from the Uthan through the interior glass in option A.",
  "Z22": "In this 3D proposal: the making line on the only solid wall of the design-wing entrance (the corridor walls are glass, so the labs behind them are the exhibit): one River to Home basket in six steps, from hogla leaves to the collection. Illustrative objects.",
  "Z05": "Planned: digital export and order centre beside reception."
 },
 "branding": {
  "pageTitle": "Bengal Earth Lab - concept proposal",
  "eyebrow": "Bengal Earth Lab · From Rural Hands to Global Homes",
